        "text": "The immutability of smart contracts also makes fixing any mistakes very difficult. For example, millions of dollars worth of Ether was stolen when a decentralized autonomous organization called the DAO was hacked in 2016. The hackers took advantage of flaws in its Smart contract code. Since the smart contract was immutable, it was challenging for developers to fix the code, and it was impossible to reverse the fraudulent transaction on the blockchain. This eventually led to a hard fork giving birth to two separate Ethereum chains. Let's move on to dapps. As you probably guessed by now, dapps are applications that run on blockchain networks. Dapps can perform functions that are similar to applications on your phone or computer, but the backend system is different.",
        "start": 880,
        "end": 49220,
        "confidence": 0.98458475,
